{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["When the Most High gave nations their heritage — that He gave them inheritances." "When He separated the sons of man — after the death of Noah, in the days of Abraham, for it is written there: משם נפרדו איי הגוים איש ללשונו, and there you will find that He set the borders of peoples. The children of Canaan, twelve, corresponding to the number of the children of Jacob, who were twelve — for you will find Canaan and his eleven sons, twelve, and it is written there: ויהי גבול הכנעני מצידון וגו׳ — because all these were for Israel, but for all the other sons of Noah He specified no border. And further I have found several approaches in the midrash to the number of the children of Israel — for Canaan and his sons are likewise twelve."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:46.298816489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}